WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.553 --> 00:00:15.196
Kevin, Nadine, and Dad looked at the huge tree lying in their backyard.

2
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.502
can't believe the storm blew our tree down," said Nadine.

3
00:00:26.703 --> 00:00:28.024
Tears filled her eyes.

4
00:00:30.748 --> 00:00:34.071
"I loved climbing that tree," Kevin said sadly.

5
00:00:36.653 --> 00:00:37.474
Dad sighed.

6
00:00:41.197 --> 00:00:43.479
old oak tree was here when my dad built this house."

7
00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.782
A truck pulled into the driveway.

8
00:00:49.184 --> 00:00:51.065
Workers with chainsaws got out.

9
00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:55.569
The workers cut off the small branches.

10
00:00:58.832 --> 00:01:01.113
Then they cut into the thick trunk.

11
00:01:02.313 --> 00:01:03.834
Sawdust filled the air.

12
00:01:05.074 --> 00:01:08.196
With a giant crack, the trunk broke in half.

13
00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.861
has rings of wood inside!"

14
00:01:21.421 --> 00:01:22.222
said Nadine.

15
00:01:24.663 --> 00:01:27.904
"Most trees add one ring every year," said Dad.

16
00:01:29.312 --> 00:01:31.493
"We can count the rings to find the tree's age."

17
00:01:32.713 --> 00:01:35.074
Kevin and Nadine took turns counting.

18
00:01:51.201 --> 00:01:54.062
tree was 213 years old!"

19
00:01:54.622 --> 00:01:55.423
Nadine said.

20
00:01:55.443 --> 00:02:02.233
"That's right, and it has a tale to tell," said a lady behind them.

21
00:02:02.253 --> 00:02:04.194
"You must be Dr.

22
00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.714
Learner," said Dad.

23
00:02:06.915 --> 00:02:08.275
She smiled at the kids.

24
00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:13.837
"Dr. Learner is taking a slab for the Tree Ring Lab.

25
00:02:14.357 --> 00:02:17.238
It's at the University of Arizona," said Dad.

26
00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:23.660
Dr. Learner explained that the Tree Ring Lab had two million tree samples.

27
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:29.362
"Trees build a picture of the earth's history," she said.

28
00:02:32.583 --> 00:02:34.984
She pointed to a thin ring in the trunk.

29
00:02:36.045 --> 00:02:40.707
"This year had little rain, so your tree did not grow very much."

30
00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:46.049
"Cool!" said Nadine, pointing to a thick ring.

31
00:02:46.069 --> 00:02:48.470
"This year was rainy."

32
00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:52.351
"Trees are like a weather calendar!"

33
00:02:52.712 --> 00:02:53.332
said Kevin.

34
00:02:55.644 --> 00:02:57.586
"More than that," said Dr.

35
00:02:57.626 --> 00:03:00.548
Learner. She pointed to a twisted ring.

36
00:03:01.869 --> 00:03:06.433
"This scar shows that something unusual happened—likely a fire.

37
00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:09.435
Trees can tell us about big events.

38
00:03:10.776 --> 00:03:14.479
A tree would grow less if a hurricane blew off its leaves.

39
00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.801
Or if a volcano erupted."

40
00:03:19.503 --> 00:03:20.324
Kevin laughed.

41
00:03:23.276 --> 00:03:25.557
"People would remember a volcano eruption!"

42
00:03:26.978 --> 00:03:29.880
Dr. Learner showed them a picture of a tree slab.

43
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.181
It was twice as tall as a man.

44
00:03:33.201 --> 00:03:36.683
"This tree grew from 212 to 1913."

45
00:03:36.743 --> 00:03:38.004
"Whoa! That's 1,701 years!"

46
00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:38.824
said Nadine.

47
00:03:43.107 --> 00:03:44.327
Kevin shrugged.

48
00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:57.404
"Okay, maybe trees are better than people at remembering things."

49
00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.586
Dr. Learner smiled.

50
00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:07.092
"The oldest living tree is five thousand years old."

51
00:04:08.153 --> 00:04:09.974
Nadine's eyes grew wide.

52
00:04:09.995 --> 00:04:14.598
"How do you know that without cutting it down?"

53
00:04:14.618 --> 00:04:19.983
"We use a tool that drills a tiny hole," said Dr.

54
00:04:21.804 --> 00:04:23.405
Learner. "It doesn't hurt the tree."

55
00:04:31.513 --> 00:04:32.594
The workers finished.

56
00:04:43.304 --> 00:04:44.705
The backyard was quiet.

57
00:04:45.546 --> 00:04:47.688
It looked strange without the tall tree.

58
00:04:49.876 --> 00:04:52.177
Nadine spied something near the fence.

59
00:04:54.018 --> 00:04:56.580
"Look! Our tree had a baby!"

60
00:05:00.302 --> 00:05:01.603
The family hurried over.

61
00:05:02.783 --> 00:05:04.044
The tree was tiny.

62
00:05:04.064 --> 00:05:09.667
"I wonder what stories this tree will tell in the future," said Kevin.

63
00:05:11.188 --> 00:05:13.609
"I don't think you'll find out," said Dad.

64
00:05:13.629 --> 00:05:18.072
"But maybe your grandchildren or your great-grandchildren will."
